        "file": "git-linux-ai-foundations/git-foundations/stash/artifact.html",
        "line": 253
      },
      "claim": "The lesson states without qualification that git stash pop reapplies the newest entry and removes it from the stack. If applying the stash conflicts, Git leaves the entry in the stash list; the unconditional rule is technically false and can mislead learners during the exact recovery case where retention matters.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "url": "https://git-scm.com/docs/git-stash",
          "section": "pop: applying the state can fail with conflicts; in this case it is not removed from the stash list",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-12T22:51:59Z",
          "textSha256": "5decb52d316639446f5060c8b813398a62c9d9e54d44c7cc6d014cdc5e96cabc"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Qualify the teaching, recap, cheat sheet, Markdown, and GIFT pop item: pop removes the entry after a successful apply; if conflicts prevent a clean apply, the entry remains and the learner resolves conflicts before dropping it manually.",
      "reviewedSha256": "1bbe3b3b9a8c0381ef58113fed506a992fccf434738ecbeee5f5803e19b2130e"
    },
    {
      "id": "sme-git-002",
      "severity": "low",
      "location": {
        "file": "git-linux-ai-foundations/git-foundations/merge-conflicts/artifact.html",
        "line": 253
      },
      "claim": "The recap turns the lesson's same-lines example into a complete definition: 'A conflict happens when both branches changed the same lines.' Same-area textual edits are a common conflict, but Git's actual condition is that the merge cannot be resolved automatically; conflicts are not limited to this one shape.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "url": "https://git-scm.com/docs/git-merge",
          "section": "DESCRIPTION and HOW CONFLICTS ARE PRESENTED: a merge stops for a conflict that cannot be resolved automatically; same-area changes describe conflicted textual hunks",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-12T22:51:43Z",
          "textSha256": "5e79338714ddddad7dee4d530e221023f5611b5cd0ce17126a6e6066ad8a448c"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Change the categorical recap and matching GIFT feedback to 'A common conflict happens when both branches change the same area and Git cannot combine the changes automatically.' Keep the existing same-line exercise and marker instruction unchanged.",
      "reviewedSha256": "5c8fe68e9e7361554e6994022cccfdca85d2659de9a6c947515519045b83541d"
